 "title": "A two-level partition function",
 "caption": "The partition function q = Σ e^(−Eᵢ/kT) counts the states thermally available. For two levels a gap ε apart, q = 1 + e^(−ε/kT): just 1 when kT ≪ ε (only the ground state is used) and approaching 2 when kT ≫ ε (both equally).",
